  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry and tranquil weather will continue through this \nweekend.\n\nHigh pressure will continue to dominate the weather across our region \nthrough the weekend. A moisture-starved cold front will finish \ncrossing the region this afternoon. Behind the front, an incoming \ncooler air mass will bring some increase in lake-induced\ninstability, with some scattered to broken lake induced cloud \ncover eventually developing tonight and into Friday morning. A \nnortherly flow will also allow for some upslope clouds to also \ndevelop. Moisture profiles are very limited, so there will be no\nthreat for precipitation.\n\nHigh pressure at the surface and aloft will continue to build to\nthe east and settle over the Northeast Friday and this weekend.\nDry weather and clear to partly cloudy sky are expected as \nstabilizing subsidence accompanies the ridge. Daily highs should\nmoderate from mainly the 50s to 60F Friday to the mid 50s to upper\n60s on Sunday as a more southerly flow develops on the western \nside of the ridge.\n\nThe environment should remain favorable for localized and shallow \nfog in the Black River Valley, Western Southern Tier river valleys, \nand the lake valleys of the Finger Lakes Region between about 12 AM \nand 9 AM EDT Friday through Sunday.",
